{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.50:0.4", "PA_thag_1.50:1.1"], "en": "Vimala Thera’s Verse: “The rain falls and the wind blows;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.50:1.2"], "en": "lightning flashes across the sky.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.50:1.3"], "en": "“Discursive thoughts have subsided;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.50:1.4"], "en": "my mind is well-composed.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.50:1.5"], "en": "… Thus spoke the Elder Vimala.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.50:1.6"], "en": "The fifth chapter.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.50:2.0"], "en": "Its summary verse:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.50:2.1"], "en": "Sirivaḍḍha, the elder Revata, ...", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.50:2.2"], "en": "Sumaṅgala and Sānu,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.50:2.3"], "en": "Ramaṇīyavihārī,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.50:2.4"], "en": "Samiddhi, Ujjaya, and Sañjaya;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.50:2.5"], "en": "That elder is delightful,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.50:2.6"], "en": "stainless, and free from conflict.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"}
